# XSH dirfd()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.

assertion  XSH.dirfd.001
anchor     functions/dirfd.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2008
says       dirfd() of a stream from opendir("d") returns a descriptor that
           fstat() shows to be d.
test       t/001-dirfd.c

assertion  XSH.dirfd.002
anchor     functions/dirfd.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2024
says       dirfd() returns the same descriptor each time; for a stream from
           fdopendir(fd) it returns fd; after closedir() the descriptor
           dirfd() returned is no longer open.
test       t/002-own-descriptor.c
